      "message": "dumpcap: remove some code `#if`ed out since 2005.\n\nSome code was introduced in 5d404864f204147ede0cb6e19c64e06ebdb85496\nthat was `#if`ed out; the commit message said it was adding logging, and\nall the other changes appear to be logging-related, so that might have\nbeen an unintentional commit of personal experimental/testing code.\n\nIt's been unused since at least 2005, so we can probably remove it.\n\nWhile we're at it, when testing whether a capture loop terminated due to\nan error or a `pcap_breakloop()` call, test for errors other than\n`PCAP_ERROR_BREAK` rather than testing for `PCAP_ERROR`, so we treat\nerrors other than `PCAP_ERROR` and `PCAP_ERROR_BREAK` as errors.\n\nAI-Assisted: no\n",
